# The HTTP server benchmark, native release: the server whose CPU per
# request runner.js reads while Node clients load it over loopback. Not run
# by CI; the numbers are for reading. From the repository root:
#
#   haxe tests/perf/http/perf-http.hxml
#   node tests/perf/http/runner.js --exe export/perf-http/release/PerfHttpServer.exe \
#     --scenario mw --load http -- --conns 32 --procs 4 --headers browser
#
# suite.js runs a list of cases (cases/*.json) with their repetitions
# interleaved; build-stage.ps1 keeps one build per stage for before and after.
# Windows: the runner pins with `start /affinity`, the server reads its CPU
# with GetProcessTimes.
-cp tests/perf/http
-cp src
-D windows
-D HXCPP_M64
-main PerfHttpServer
--cpp export/perf-http/release
